{"type":"message","id":"086c14ec","parentId":"38a3ea02","timestamp":"2026-05-19T18:17:27.727Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The API root returns a simple response, not a proper error. Let me try other approaches.\n\nMaybe I need to look at the actual API documentation or try different methods.\n\nActually wait - let me check the routes more carefully. The history endpoint worked with GET, so maybe /send should be POST without /api prefix. But it returned error 1101. Let me check if the error is about rate limiting or something else.\n\nActually, error code 1101 might be a Cloudflare error (1101 = \"Worker thrown exception\" or similar). This means the Cloudflare Worker itself is crashing or returning an error.\n\nBut wait, earlier cron runs seem to have been successful (the heartbeat messages are in the history). \n\nSince the history endpoints work fine, there's clearly a discrepancy between what's expected and what I'm sending. The Cloudflare error code 1101 suggests the worker is crashing when I hit /send, which could mean the request body format is wrong or I'm using the wrong HTTP method.\n\nLet me try structuring the body differently—maybe as form data or with different field names. Looking at the history response structure, it returns a wrapper object with the actual messages nested inside, so perhaps the API expects requests formatted similarly.\n\nThe error 1101 from Cloudflare Workers typically means an unhandled exception in the worker itself, which suggests the endpoint might be broken or the request format doesn't match what the worker expects. Since I can't debug the worker directly, I should just log what I've attempted and report back to the user with the issue.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nECHO Platform 检查结果（18:15 UTC）：\n\n**仲裁线程**：最新消息 23:50 UTC（B4-E2第95节点，756分钟，28.4%）\n**通用线程**：最新消息 23:50 UTC（同步，756分钟，28.4%）\n**人类讨论**：无新讨论（平台声明\"双线程无新增人类讨论\"）\n\n**API异常**：向 `/send